[
    {
        "content": "<p>We can write f(x) = (f(x)+f(-x))/2 + (f(x)-f(-x))/2, where the first term is even and the second term is odd.  Is there a theorem for this in Mathlib?  Do we have something more general?</p>",
        "id": 614929023,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Kielstra",
        "timestamp": 1786003712
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This topic was moved here from <a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"217875\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Any.20function.20can.20be.20written.20as.20odd.20plus.20even\">#Is there code for X? &gt; Any function can be written as odd plus even</a> by <span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"920569\">Michael Kielstra</span>.</p>",
        "id": 614929097,
        "sender_full_name": "Notification Bot",
        "timestamp": 1786003734
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I don't think we do. You could add it somewhere near <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Function.Even#doc\">docs#Function.Even</a> maybe? and you can take a look at <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=StarModule.selfAdjointPart_add_skewAdjointPart#doc\">docs#StarModule.selfAdjointPart_add_skewAdjointPart</a> for how a similar result can be structured.</p>",
        "id": 614934560,
        "sender_full_name": "Luigi Massacci",
        "timestamp": 1786005475
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The proofs are very easy, so I am not sure we need additional definitions for this.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Analysis</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Normed</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Operator</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Basic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- just to get the tactics</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- obviously holds more generally, but the proofs such not be affected</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- or `field_simp; ring`</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Function</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Even</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- `simp; ring` instead of `grind` also works</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Function</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Odd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 614937838,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Doll",
        "timestamp": 1786006473
    }
]